  "final_message": "Refunding a paid invoice should now work. The 24 existing tests pass, but I didn't add a test that reproduces the refund bug, so the fix itself isn't covered.\n\n**Root cause:** in `refund_invoice` (`billing/refunds.py:41`), the code called `successful_payments(ctx, invoice[\"customer_id\"])`. That function looks payments up by invoice ID, so it searched using a customer ID and found nothing. The refund loop then never ran. If the invoice had no applied credit, it raised \"invoice has no successful payment to refund\".\n\n**Fix:** it now passes `invoice_id`.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` in the repository root: `{\"file\": \"refunds.py\", \"function\": \"refund_invoice\"}`.",
